bisectQ GAINED A processCode ERROR IN THE fbGen REPAIR PASS

On 2026-08-24 the scaffold emitter in incant/f31 and its eleven copies was
repaired for families A, B and C (commit e8e8619). Eleven of the twelve patched
files either improved or held. One did not.

    file                    processCode errors before -> after   exit
    incant/fixBisect                    1 -> 0                   0 -> 0
    minionWork/probeM3                  1 -> 0                   0 -> 0
    minionWork/probeExitExam            4 -> 1                 139 -> 139
    incant/walkPhase                   49 -> 55                 139 -> 0
    incant/phaseProbe                   0 -> 0                   0 -> 0
    incant/bisectQ                      0 -> 1                   0 -> 0     <-- this

WHY IT IS EXPECTED THAT THESE MOVE AT ALL, so the row is not misread as a
regression in the repair: every one of these files EMBEDS a copy of the emitter
that was changed, and their whole purpose is to compile generated bodies. Their
output moving is the repair working. What singles bisectQ out is DIRECTION -- it
is the only file that went from clean to not-clean.

WHAT IS NOT KNOWN

Whether the new error is collateral from the mechanical edit (the patch inserted
a counter field, a bump action and a tag-match action into each copy, and
bisectQ's surrounding shape may differ from the others in a way the patch did
not respect), or whether bisectQ is compiling a rule that the repaired emitter
now emits DIFFERENTLY and worse.

⚠ "LIKELY COLLATERAL FROM THE FIXTURE EDIT" IS THE STANDING GUESS AND IT IS
RECORDED AS A GUESS. This project's ledger says structural claims hold here and
causal ones are a coin flip until run; nothing below has been run.

